      "text": [
        " «مَنْ أَخْرَجَ اَلْفِطْرَةَ» فَقِيلَ لَهُ «وَ ذَكَرَ اِسْمَ رَبِّهِ فَصَلّٰى» قَالَ «خَرَجَ إِلَى اَلْجَبَّانَةِ فَصَلَّى."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1474 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) was asked about the verse of Allah (swt), the Exalted, \"Successful indeed are those who purify themselves,\" (Surah Al-A'la 87:14).\nImam (as) said: \"This refers to the one who gives the Fitrah (charity for breaking the fast).\"\nHe was then asked about the verse, \"and remember the Name of their Lord (azj), and pray.\" (Surah Al-A'la 87:15).\nImam (as) said: \"This means going out to the prayer ground and performing the prayer.\""
        ]
      }
